WEBVTT

00:42.042 --> 00:45.963
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:46.880 --> 00:48.924
Just like in the "Three Bears" song,

00:49.758 --> 00:52.678
the world made it seem like
a family should consist of three.

00:55.722 --> 00:58.559
But just like having two eyes
and two ears…

00:58.642 --> 00:59.685
You missed a spot.

00:59.768 --> 01:01.687
…two always felt more natural to me.

01:01.770 --> 01:03.355
My dad and I.

01:05.399 --> 01:06.316
Hi.

01:06.400 --> 01:07.609
But one day,

01:08.360 --> 01:09.361
two became three.

01:10.654 --> 01:12.281
Hey, guess what!

01:12.364 --> 01:14.283
I just saw the old unmarried bat
in the hallway.

01:14.366 --> 01:16.410
- Yeom Bun-hong!
- Our fifth-grade teacher?

01:16.493 --> 01:18.745
- Is she a parent?
- We became another set of three.

01:18.829 --> 01:20.455
- But she's not married.
- Ho-su.

01:20.539 --> 01:21.790
But for some reason,

01:22.541 --> 01:25.377
it just made me feel
like I had three eyes instead.

01:25.460 --> 01:27.045
Why is she going?

01:27.129 --> 01:28.088
Ho-su.

01:28.171 --> 01:32.217
Why can't it be just us at Mom's memorial?
It's always been the two of us!

01:32.301 --> 01:33.719
Ho-su…

01:34.469 --> 01:36.555
My gosh, I'm so sorry.

01:36.638 --> 01:40.559
Something urgent came up at school,
so the two of you should go without me.

01:43.020 --> 01:44.938
- Bun-hong.
- Ironically, the day I insisted

01:45.022 --> 01:46.523
that it be just the two of us…

02:01.580 --> 02:02.789
Ho-su.

02:03.498 --> 02:04.416
Ho-su!

02:06.501 --> 02:09.254
- Help! He's awake! Ho-su!
- …we actually did become

02:09.338 --> 02:10.505
two again.

02:10.589 --> 02:11.715
Bye.

02:12.257 --> 02:13.342
See you tomorrow.

02:13.425 --> 02:15.719
Stop humiliating the family.

02:15.802 --> 02:17.512
You want to raise someone else's kid?

02:17.596 --> 02:19.890
What are you going to tell people?

02:19.973 --> 02:22.726
She's right! Don't just
decide this on your own, Bun-hong.

02:22.809 --> 02:25.187
No one will blame you
if you decide not to raise him.

02:25.270 --> 02:28.065
Listen to us. It's not easy
to raise a kid that isn't yours.

02:28.148 --> 02:29.399
No, it became just one.

02:29.483 --> 02:31.902
You'll have to take care of him
his whole life.

02:31.985 --> 02:34.237
- One broken piece.
- Why take on that burden?

02:43.163 --> 02:44.247
Excuse me.

02:44.831 --> 02:46.333
You're Bun-hong, right?

02:46.416 --> 02:49.127
Remember me?
I'm Kim Ok-hui from Sinsong Girls' High.

02:49.211 --> 02:50.420
Oh my gosh! Ok-hui!

02:50.504 --> 02:51.672
- My goodness.
- My gosh.

02:51.755 --> 02:55.936
I was wondering who was moving in
next door. I can't believe it's you!

02:56.009 --> 02:58.136
- My gosh! What a surprise.
- My goodness.

02:59.221 --> 03:00.639
- Is he your son?
- Yes.

03:00.722 --> 03:03.642
I didn't even hear you got married.
And now you've got a son this big?

03:03.725 --> 03:06.103
Goodness, I forgot
to tell you I got married.

03:07.562 --> 03:12.025
Nice to meet you. Your mom
and I went to the same high school.

03:12.109 --> 03:14.194
- Gosh, he's so handsome.
- That's when I started

03:14.277 --> 03:16.905
trying my best not to become a burden.

03:18.240 --> 03:19.658
Just like my ears,

03:21.326 --> 03:23.161
which seemed fine on the outside.

03:23.662 --> 03:26.164
Ho-su, why did you take out
your hearing aid?

03:26.248 --> 03:28.750
Even if it doesn't work well,
you should use it.

03:28.834 --> 03:31.294
I feel more comfortable
hearing with just one ear.

03:33.422 --> 03:34.840
As long as I pretended…

03:36.717 --> 03:38.385
that I was fine,

03:40.345 --> 03:42.889
I'd seem whole on the outside.

03:44.808 --> 03:49.730
EPISODE 8
AN UNCONVENTIONAL WHOLE

03:49.813 --> 03:51.857
WAITING AREA
TICKET COUNTER

03:59.030 --> 04:00.240
I've liked you…

04:01.867 --> 04:03.160
for a long time.

04:04.327 --> 04:05.454
More than you know.

04:06.997 --> 04:08.373
Me too.

04:30.687 --> 04:32.147
You should go inside.

04:32.814 --> 04:34.191
You must be cold.

04:34.983 --> 04:36.067
What?

04:39.738 --> 04:42.365
- Yes, okay.
- Okay.

04:46.870 --> 04:47.871
See you.

04:47.954 --> 04:49.039
See you.

05:00.967 --> 05:03.094
What are we now?

05:03.804 --> 05:06.973
Since I said, "Me too,"
are we officially a couple now?

05:07.682 --> 05:10.101
Or maybe we're not a couple yet.

05:12.813 --> 05:15.774
- Sorry. Have you been waiting long?
- No, it's okay.

05:16.483 --> 05:18.568
Why are you wet though? Is that sweat?

05:18.652 --> 05:20.153
No, I just washed my face.

05:20.695 --> 05:22.572
I was rushing,
so I didn't have time to wash.

05:22.656 --> 05:26.243
I told you that you didn't need to come.

05:26.326 --> 05:28.745
You had to wake up early because of me.

05:28.829 --> 05:31.122
Of course I needed to come.
You're leaving.

05:32.165 --> 05:33.250
Jeez.

05:33.750 --> 05:35.669
You didn't have to come.

05:38.421 --> 05:42.133
Will you be going to work instead
of Mi-rae again when you get to Seoul?

05:42.217 --> 05:44.386
Yes, but it's all going to be over soon.

05:45.136 --> 05:47.889
You must be tired.
You probably didn't get enough sleep.

05:49.266 --> 05:52.978
What? I slept really well.
I passed out as soon as I hit the pillow.

05:54.563 --> 05:55.772
That's good.

05:56.731 --> 05:58.400
I had a hard time falling asleep.

06:04.990 --> 06:06.074
Hey.

06:08.451 --> 06:09.911
- Are we…
- Yes?

06:10.996 --> 06:12.038
Well…

06:16.042 --> 06:17.878
When are we seeing each other again?

06:18.837 --> 06:21.756
I'm planning to return
as soon as my mom gets discharged.

06:21.840 --> 06:23.466
I'll call you when I'm in Seoul.

06:23.550 --> 06:25.218
Okay.

06:27.929 --> 06:28.930
Hey…

06:29.639 --> 06:30.557
Yes?

06:33.351 --> 06:34.686
Have a…

06:38.982 --> 06:41.026
- All right.
- Have a safe trip.

06:41.776 --> 06:42.819
Thanks.

06:43.320 --> 06:44.905
- Go home now.
- Okay.

06:44.988 --> 06:46.573
Bye, then.

06:49.451 --> 06:51.953
Did we seriously just shake hands?
That's so lame.

06:54.414 --> 06:57.584
Yes, the amount is right.
I'll help you with the payment now.

06:58.585 --> 07:00.754
You usually come right on time.

07:00.837 --> 07:02.172
But this time, you were late,

07:02.255 --> 07:05.008
so I was worried that
something had happened to you.

07:05.091 --> 07:08.053
I was a little sick.

07:08.136 --> 07:09.179
SEONHAM MENTAL NURSING HOME

07:09.262 --> 07:12.724
Is there someone I can put down
as your emergency contact?

07:12.807 --> 07:14.559
I need to have one on file

07:14.643 --> 07:17.395
just in case something
like this happens again.

07:17.479 --> 07:19.731
As I mentioned before,

07:19.814 --> 07:22.776
I'm the only family he's got.

07:22.859 --> 07:26.780
There's something called
an adult guardianship program.

07:26.863 --> 07:27.948
What?

07:28.031 --> 07:29.991
It's called an adult guardianship program.

07:30.075 --> 07:33.954
You can designate a guardian
ahead of time, even if they're not family.

07:34.037 --> 07:37.791
You should read it over
and give it some thought.

07:39.459 --> 07:40.502
Thank you.

07:40.585 --> 07:42.212
Take care, ma'am.

07:42.295 --> 07:43.797
JOIN THE ADULT GUARDIANSHIP PROGRAM!

07:44.422 --> 07:46.883
- Mom, I got you discharged.
- Okay.

07:46.967 --> 07:49.970
Leave it. I told you
that I'd pack your things.

07:50.053 --> 07:51.262
Okay.

07:52.013 --> 07:55.225
I didn't want to waste
the valuable time I have with you packing.

07:57.394 --> 07:59.854
Ok-hui, do you want to use
this humidifier?

07:59.938 --> 08:02.816
I'm getting discharged today, too.
Take it with you.

08:03.316 --> 08:05.235
I have one too.

08:05.318 --> 08:09.322
Ho-su said he'd get you discharged
with me. Why are you refusing?

08:10.031 --> 08:13.201
You're not the only one with a kid.
My daughter's coming too.

08:13.284 --> 08:14.411
We'll get going, then.

08:14.494 --> 08:16.371
- Mom.
- What?

08:17.789 --> 08:18.915
Jeez.

08:19.958 --> 08:21.835
Ho-su, are you sick?

08:22.919 --> 08:25.839
No, I'm fine. Why?

08:25.922 --> 08:27.716
You don't have a fever?

08:27.799 --> 08:30.343
You always get really sick
when the seasons change.

08:30.427 --> 08:32.554
You should see a doctor since you're here.

08:33.596 --> 08:35.765
That was only when I was a kid.
I'm fine now.

08:35.849 --> 08:37.517
- Still…
- Ms. Bun-hong.

08:38.143 --> 08:39.185
My goodness!

08:39.269 --> 08:41.813
My gosh, Ms. Su-yeong.
It's been such a long time!

08:42.439 --> 08:43.648
You look ready to pop!

08:44.357 --> 08:45.734
When did you say you were due?

08:45.817 --> 08:47.652
- Next month.
- Gosh.

08:47.736 --> 08:49.112
Are you her son?

08:49.195 --> 08:50.280
Yes, hello.

08:50.363 --> 08:53.241
You're just as handsome as she said.

08:53.324 --> 08:56.953
She told me a lot about you.

08:57.037 --> 09:00.623
My goodness,
I didn't talk about him that much.

09:01.958 --> 09:04.169
I hope I give birth to a son like you.

09:04.252 --> 09:07.005
It's a little late,
but tell me your prenatal care tips.

09:07.088 --> 09:08.089
What?

09:08.590 --> 09:12.177
Goodness, there are no special tips.

09:12.802 --> 09:15.305
Just relax. That's the best prenatal care.

09:15.388 --> 09:17.724
What was the conception dream
for your son?

09:17.807 --> 09:20.435
Many people around me
have had conception dreams for my baby,

09:20.518 --> 09:22.771
and I'm struggling to decide
which to go with.

09:23.313 --> 09:26.107
My son's conception dream was…

09:27.233 --> 09:29.486
a giant lotus flower blooming

09:30.153 --> 09:33.239
in the middle of a big lake.

09:33.323 --> 09:35.784
That's why they named me Ho-su,
meaning "lake."

09:35.867 --> 09:38.536
My goodness,
even your conception dream is amazing.

09:42.123 --> 09:44.042
Let's talk more about that in person.

09:44.918 --> 09:46.294
Text me the address.

09:48.838 --> 09:49.881
Okay.

09:51.966 --> 09:53.927
Sir, we're ready for the meeting.

09:54.010 --> 09:55.178
Okay.

09:55.261 --> 09:57.555
- Let's all go to the meeting.
- Yes, sir.

10:11.366 --> 10:12.779
REDIAL

10:17.200 --> 10:19.953
Kim Jin-gyu of Sihan Construction's
Business Development speaking.

10:20.036 --> 10:21.079
Tae-i!

10:22.497 --> 10:23.540
Hello.

10:23.623 --> 10:25.583
They just started the meeting.

10:25.667 --> 10:26.751
Already?

10:36.886 --> 10:38.596
Did Mi-rae return to Seoul?

10:38.680 --> 10:41.474
She left early this morning to go to work.

10:41.975 --> 10:44.978
Gosh, I told her to go back yesterday.
She must be tired.

10:45.979 --> 10:49.774
Why did you tell her that I got hurt
when she's so busy?

10:50.400 --> 10:52.318
She's family, so she should know.

10:52.402 --> 10:54.362
She doesn't have to!

10:54.445 --> 10:56.823
Jeez. You don't know how to keep a secret.

10:57.699 --> 11:00.535
I'm going to visit Seoul soon.

11:01.119 --> 11:02.287
Seoul?

11:02.370 --> 11:04.080
You went recently, though.

11:04.581 --> 11:06.332
Mi-rae told me to visit her.

11:07.542 --> 11:08.626
She did?

11:11.254 --> 11:12.505
By the way,

11:12.589 --> 11:15.508
- why did Ho-su come here?
- What?

11:15.592 --> 11:17.635
I heard he came here to talk to you.

11:17.719 --> 11:19.137
What did you two talk about?

11:20.889 --> 11:24.225
What exactly happened
between you and Park Sang-yeong?

11:25.059 --> 11:27.187
It was nothing important.

11:27.270 --> 11:29.647
He just asked how I was doing.

11:29.731 --> 11:32.984
He came all the way here
to ask how you're doing? That's silly.

11:33.067 --> 11:35.361
Gosh, he must have a lot of time
on his hands.

11:35.445 --> 11:38.156
He used to be so busy. Jeez.

11:38.865 --> 11:42.493
Bun-hong acted like
it was the end of the world

11:42.577 --> 11:44.787
when Ho-su quit his job.

11:44.871 --> 11:47.582
But now that he has
more free time to see her,

11:47.665 --> 11:51.044
she's even happier than
when he had a job. Go figure.

11:51.961 --> 11:54.631
Mom, how would you feel
if Mi-rae did the same thing?

11:55.298 --> 11:56.216
What do you mean?

11:56.299 --> 11:59.844
What if she were to quit her job
like Ho-su and spend more time with you?

11:59.928 --> 12:02.472
Hey! Don't say such ridiculous things.

12:02.555 --> 12:05.516
He's a lawyer,
not just an ordinary office worker.

12:07.852 --> 12:10.480
Having one unemployed daughter
is more than enough.

12:11.147 --> 12:12.106
Jeez.

12:18.404 --> 12:19.489
A favor?

12:20.156 --> 12:24.494
I'm sorry to bother you when I told you
I didn't need your help before,

12:25.078 --> 12:27.789
but I have no one else to ask.

12:29.916 --> 12:32.377
I'm happy to help with whatever you need.

12:32.460 --> 12:34.420
What's the favor, though?

12:34.504 --> 12:36.339
If you tell me what you need,

12:37.715 --> 12:39.342
then I'll have it ready.

12:40.093 --> 12:45.056
It's a long story to tell over the phone.

12:45.723 --> 12:49.227
It's not urgent, so let's talk in person.

12:49.852 --> 12:51.771
Do you have time on Monday?

12:56.317 --> 12:57.986
Mom, what are you doing?

12:58.069 --> 13:00.738
I'm just cleaning the electric blanket
before I put it on the bed.

13:00.822 --> 13:02.699
It's dusty
since I haven't used it in a while.

13:02.782 --> 13:03.950
I'll do it.

13:04.492 --> 13:05.743
You should've told me.

13:05.827 --> 13:08.204
How did you get this out by yourself?

13:08.288 --> 13:12.250
I thought maybe you weren't feeling well
because the house was chilly.

13:12.333 --> 13:13.793
Wipe it for me, then.

13:21.509 --> 13:22.593
What are you doing now?

13:22.677 --> 13:24.012
Well…

13:24.095 --> 13:25.972
I'm going to make some baesuk.

13:26.055 --> 13:28.182
It always made you feel better
when you had a cold.

13:28.266 --> 13:30.852
Mom, you're the patient.
Why are you taking care of me?

13:30.935 --> 13:33.062
Just don't make it.

13:33.146 --> 13:34.689
It's very easy to make.

13:35.565 --> 13:38.484
I just need to boil everything in a pot.

13:41.404 --> 13:42.613
- Mom.
- Yes?

13:43.573 --> 13:45.033
I'll just go back this weekend.

13:46.701 --> 13:47.744
What?

13:48.578 --> 13:50.038
Why so soon?

13:50.705 --> 13:51.831
Since you came home,

13:52.332 --> 13:54.709
you haven't been able to rest
because of me.

13:55.335 --> 13:57.587
Okay, I see what you mean.

13:59.088 --> 14:00.757
I'll stop. I won't do anything.

14:02.008 --> 14:03.676
You said that earlier too.

14:04.844 --> 14:05.970
I think…

14:06.929 --> 14:09.682
you'll only be able to rest
comfortably without me here.

14:14.896 --> 14:15.980
Then…

14:16.773 --> 14:18.858
let me pack up some food for you.

14:18.941 --> 14:22.737
I was going to send it to Seoul,
but this is perfect!

14:23.988 --> 14:26.991
Mom, I'm okay.

14:27.575 --> 14:29.827
I can't just let you go back empty-handed

14:29.911 --> 14:32.914
after everything I put you through.

14:32.997 --> 14:35.041
People will gossip if I don't do anything.

14:36.042 --> 14:37.043
Do you…

14:39.170 --> 14:40.671
still feel uncomfortable?

14:43.132 --> 14:44.384
What?

14:44.467 --> 14:46.719
I'm all grown up now.

14:48.221 --> 14:51.933
You don't have to try as hard
as you did before.

14:53.476 --> 14:56.145
Mom, from now on…

14:58.648 --> 15:00.733
just focus on taking care of yourself.

15:19.043 --> 15:22.338
I guess you don't get many customers
in wheelchairs here.

15:23.423 --> 15:25.007
I don't serve solo diners.

15:25.508 --> 15:27.510
I just came to introduce myself.

15:28.344 --> 15:31.180
I'm currently a consultant for KFMC--

15:31.264 --> 15:33.307
If you're not a customer, get out.

15:33.391 --> 15:34.934
Hyeon Sang-wol.

15:38.646 --> 15:40.106
You know her, right?

15:44.193 --> 15:45.486
Who are you?

15:47.238 --> 15:49.657
I guess I've piqued your interest now.

15:51.576 --> 15:54.203
My name is Lee Chung-gu. I'm a lawyer.

16:05.214 --> 16:06.716
HIGH-QUALITY STRAWBERRY MANUAL

16:13.764 --> 16:15.016
You scared me!

16:15.808 --> 16:16.767
"You scared me!"

16:17.894 --> 16:18.936
What were you doing?

16:20.271 --> 16:21.314
Here.

16:29.655 --> 16:32.283
"High-quality Strawberry Manual."

16:32.366 --> 16:34.911
"Research on Breeding New Varieties."

16:34.994 --> 16:36.913
"Future Cultivation Plan."

16:36.996 --> 16:39.373
Are you from
the Rural Development Administration?

16:39.457 --> 16:42.919
You'll be doing it alone from now on,
so I figured these could be useful.

16:43.002 --> 16:45.755
If you were bringing gifts,
you should've told me.

16:45.838 --> 16:47.048
Why leave them here secretly?

16:47.131 --> 16:49.091
Are you my Secret Santa or something?

16:49.800 --> 16:51.761
I thought it'd be awkward
to say goodbye again

16:51.844 --> 16:54.430
after the handshake
and everything the other day.

16:56.182 --> 16:58.100
Why would it be awkward?

16:58.184 --> 17:01.187
I circled the block a few times,
hoping to say goodbye again.

17:01.729 --> 17:04.232
When are you going to Seoul?
Are you leaving now?

17:04.315 --> 17:06.192
Not right away, but soon.

17:07.693 --> 17:09.612
If you're not leaving today,

17:10.446 --> 17:11.781
do you want to meet up tonight?

17:13.783 --> 17:15.243
Why at night?

17:17.245 --> 17:19.747
Because the stars are visible at night.

17:23.668 --> 17:25.753
I found a great stargazing spot.

17:26.379 --> 17:28.005
Do you want to go with me later?

17:33.469 --> 17:34.679
Be careful.

17:37.848 --> 17:41.310
Are we really on our way to see stars?

17:42.728 --> 17:45.314
I'm sensing some serious distrust.

17:46.649 --> 17:47.858
We're almost there.

17:47.942 --> 17:50.570
You've been saying that for a while now.

17:51.195 --> 17:52.488
You can do it!

18:05.668 --> 18:06.836
What is it?

18:15.928 --> 18:16.929
Wow!

18:29.567 --> 18:31.360
Aren't you glad you came?

18:31.444 --> 18:33.279
You almost left without seeing this.

18:34.530 --> 18:38.159
So those same stars
are in the Seoul sky too, right?

18:38.868 --> 18:41.871
The sky is the same here
as it is in Seoul.

18:43.414 --> 18:47.084
Some things are better seen in the dark.

18:49.712 --> 18:51.922
I wonder what
it would've been like in Seoul.

18:52.965 --> 18:54.300
What do you mean?

18:55.301 --> 18:56.552
I'm talking about us.

18:57.386 --> 18:59.513
I think if we had run
into each other in Seoul,

18:59.597 --> 19:01.349
that would've been interesting too.

19:03.351 --> 19:05.853
You wouldn't have even noticed me.

19:07.271 --> 19:08.272
Why not?

19:08.856 --> 19:11.400
Even if we had met on our way
to or from work,

19:11.484 --> 19:13.861
I would've just been
like one of those many stars.

19:13.944 --> 19:15.321
Because I'm so ordinary.

19:16.280 --> 19:17.657
Never mind.

19:17.740 --> 19:20.743
You probably wouldn't have
even seen me because it's Seoul.

19:22.703 --> 19:24.121
Thank goodness we didn't.

19:24.622 --> 19:29.043
If we had, you would've said I'm annoying
and refused to even talk to me.

19:29.126 --> 19:31.253
You're only talking to me like this
because we're here.

19:31.337 --> 19:32.380
Jeez…

19:38.177 --> 19:39.261
Anyway,

19:40.179 --> 19:42.598
have you given any thought
to your future plans?

19:43.891 --> 19:44.934
Not yet.

19:47.937 --> 19:50.356
I decided to go to Seoul,

19:51.023 --> 19:53.526
but I still haven't decided
what to do once I get there.

19:53.609 --> 19:54.777
It's hard.

19:54.860 --> 19:57.738
Wouldn't it be nice if someone made
that decision for you?

19:59.448 --> 20:00.449
Yes.

20:00.991 --> 20:03.786
Is staying here an option, by any chance?

20:03.869 --> 20:06.539
There's not much I can do here.

20:06.622 --> 20:10.418
Regardless of whether I keep working
at the same place or move somewhere else,

20:11.335 --> 20:13.087
I need to keep making money.

20:13.713 --> 20:16.424
I have a lot of money.
Should I lend you some?

20:17.758 --> 20:18.843
So…

20:19.427 --> 20:22.555
this is what you were like in Seoul?

20:23.764 --> 20:26.142
I mean it when I say I want to help.

20:27.685 --> 20:30.104
Instead of rushing to make a decision,

20:30.187 --> 20:32.523
why don't you stay here
and see the strawberries grow with me

20:32.606 --> 20:35.192
while you take time
to think about your next move?

20:36.569 --> 20:39.447
I'll consider it as an option.

20:43.075 --> 20:45.536
When are you going to Seoul?
I'll give you a ride.

20:46.036 --> 20:47.204
In what?

20:47.705 --> 20:48.748
The truck.

20:50.374 --> 20:52.835
Can you even drive
on the highway with that?

20:52.918 --> 20:54.295
I don't think you can.

20:55.546 --> 20:58.758
I just sensed some serious distrust again.

21:13.105 --> 21:15.483
PHARMACY

21:15.941 --> 21:18.402
Hey, Mr. Handsome!

21:19.570 --> 21:21.864
Hey! Why did you turn around?

21:21.947 --> 21:23.908
Do you think you're handsome?

21:23.991 --> 21:25.075
Mi-ji…

21:25.159 --> 21:27.161
How did you know when I was arriving?

21:27.244 --> 21:31.165
You said you were taking the first bus.
I calculated your arrival time.

21:31.248 --> 21:35.169
It's so quiet here. I guess it's because
not many stores are open yet.

21:35.252 --> 21:37.797
Doesn't it feel like we have
the place to ourselves?

21:37.880 --> 21:40.466
Are we heading to a restaurant,
by the way?

21:41.008 --> 21:43.636
What? I was just walking.

21:45.054 --> 21:47.556
Why? Are you tired?
Do you want to sit down for a moment?

21:47.640 --> 21:49.850
No, I wasn't asking because I'm tired.

21:49.934 --> 21:52.019
Well, I'm tired.

21:52.102 --> 21:54.855
Over there!
Let's go and sit there for a minute.

22:00.236 --> 22:02.905
Wow. We've walked pretty far.

22:03.572 --> 22:07.409
If I'm not paying attention,
I can walk all the way to Gyeonggi-do.

22:07.993 --> 22:11.372
From now on, you need to tell me
to stop when you're with me.

22:11.997 --> 22:13.833
You can walk all you want.

22:13.916 --> 22:16.085
It's not that I want to walk.

22:16.627 --> 22:19.922
We walked a lot more than I realized
because I was with you.

22:24.510 --> 22:25.636
What?

22:26.428 --> 22:27.805
It just feels surreal.

22:28.681 --> 22:30.766
I can't believe
I'm here with you like this.

22:32.351 --> 22:35.020
Should I ask if we're a couple now?

22:35.104 --> 22:36.313
No, maybe I shouldn't.

22:36.397 --> 22:39.567
Am I supposed to just
go with the flow like this?

22:41.193 --> 22:42.278
What is it?

22:43.028 --> 22:45.948
You know…

22:46.824 --> 22:48.784
Are we now…

22:54.164 --> 22:55.249
Are we going to eat?

22:56.125 --> 22:57.376
Yes, we should.

22:58.377 --> 23:01.046
You must be hungry.
What do you feel like eating?

23:01.672 --> 23:03.424
Let's see what's open nearby.

23:03.966 --> 23:08.762
I think we're near Seorae Village.
Should we go there since we're close by?

23:08.846 --> 23:11.265
We can just go to any restaurant
that's open on our way.

23:11.348 --> 23:12.641
Seorae Village?

23:12.725 --> 23:14.560
Or…

23:15.144 --> 23:18.063
if we go this way,
there's the Hangang River.

23:18.147 --> 23:20.149
Should we go there? Where should we go?

23:23.777 --> 23:24.862
How about my place?

23:26.614 --> 23:27.573
What?

23:32.953 --> 23:33.954
Come in.

23:34.622 --> 23:35.581
Okay.

23:46.091 --> 23:47.557
BODY ACHE
FEVER REDUCER & PAIN RELIEVER

23:48.427 --> 23:49.345
TYLENON

23:50.387 --> 23:53.182
We just got here.
Why are you taking medication?

23:53.265 --> 23:54.558
Are you sick?

23:54.642 --> 23:56.352
It's just a supplement.

24:00.731 --> 24:01.941
Have a seat.

24:02.524 --> 24:05.194
Do you want to change
into something comfortable?

24:05.277 --> 24:09.907
Why would I change right now
in someone else's place?

24:10.658 --> 24:12.743
Isn't it a little too late to be shy now?

24:13.494 --> 24:14.954
You've slept over before.

24:16.121 --> 24:17.498
But that day…

24:20.167 --> 24:22.962
You already knew it was me back then?

24:24.129 --> 24:25.297
How long have you known?

24:26.423 --> 24:28.842
I thought it was you from the start.

24:29.635 --> 24:31.553
But it didn't make any sense,

24:32.179 --> 24:33.931
so I was confused.

24:34.014 --> 24:36.850
I couldn't tell
if Mi-rae had changed or if I had.

24:36.934 --> 24:38.310
I kept getting confused.

24:39.061 --> 24:42.356
I knew for sure
the night you showed up drunk.

24:43.899 --> 24:46.235
All the confusing and strange things

24:46.902 --> 24:50.072
made sense the moment
I realized it had been you all along.

24:53.701 --> 24:55.786
By the way, what's all that?

24:55.869 --> 24:58.288
What did you bring?

24:58.372 --> 25:00.082
Just some of my old stuff.

25:00.165 --> 25:01.875
I'm bringing things back little by little.

25:01.959 --> 25:05.254
Why? They're just going to be a burden.
You should've just left them there.

25:05.337 --> 25:08.298
It's my stuff. I should keep them here
instead of at my mom's place.

25:08.382 --> 25:11.260
Why does that matter? You're family.

25:11.343 --> 25:13.637
Your mom would be hurt if she heard that.

25:13.721 --> 25:14.888
I want…

25:15.889 --> 25:17.975
my mom to live freely now.

25:18.767 --> 25:19.977
Without any burden.

25:21.895 --> 25:23.939
When did you grow up?

25:24.023 --> 25:27.276
You used to cry your heart out
when your mom was gone for the day.

25:29.194 --> 25:32.031
Don't you remember?
It was back in high school.

25:32.114 --> 25:34.074
Your mom said
she wasn't coming home for the night,

25:34.158 --> 25:35.492
and you bawled your eyes out.

25:40.205 --> 25:41.415
Ho-su…

25:42.541 --> 25:43.959
has your fever gone down?

25:52.760 --> 25:54.094
What's all this?

25:54.178 --> 25:58.015
I thought I'd start holding
your dad's ancestral rite this year.

25:59.266 --> 26:01.018
Are you doing this for me?

26:01.101 --> 26:02.478
No.

26:02.561 --> 26:04.605
I'm doing it because I want to.

26:07.483 --> 26:09.109
Then why are there two of those?

26:12.071 --> 26:13.697
One of them is for my mom.

26:14.573 --> 26:15.657
Well…

26:16.950 --> 26:18.577
Their memorials are on the same day,

26:18.660 --> 26:20.913
so I thought it'd be nice
to do them together.

26:23.290 --> 26:24.625
Don't you want to?

26:24.708 --> 26:26.168
Should we skip it?

26:31.298 --> 26:34.176
Right…

26:34.676 --> 26:36.595
I should've realized this would upset you.

26:36.678 --> 26:37.930
I'm sorry about this.

26:38.013 --> 26:39.348
Mom…

26:42.810 --> 26:44.728
Do I make you uncomfortable?

26:44.812 --> 26:46.897
Uncomfortable? Of course not, Ho-su.

26:46.980 --> 26:48.607
Then why are you doing all this?

26:50.567 --> 26:53.445
You don't have to pretend
we're family when nobody is around.

26:56.115 --> 26:58.617
I was just doing it for you--

26:58.700 --> 27:00.077
If you care about me…

27:02.538 --> 27:04.289
then just ignore me.

27:07.209 --> 27:09.294
I don't know
if it was because of the fever

27:09.378 --> 27:11.255
or my parents' ancestral tablets,

27:12.172 --> 27:15.759
but that day, I couldn't stand being
such a burden for some reason.

27:16.969 --> 27:18.679
So for the first and last time,

27:19.972 --> 27:22.558
I said I was fine being alone.

27:27.187 --> 27:29.982
But the moment I was left alone
in that empty house,

27:31.900 --> 27:33.068
I realized…

27:34.820 --> 27:37.239
I had never been truly alone before.

27:47.457 --> 27:48.584
Hello.

27:49.209 --> 27:50.335
Hi.

27:50.919 --> 27:52.504
It's me, Bun-hong.

27:53.130 --> 27:55.340
- Are you Mi-ji or Mi-rae?
- I'm Mi-ji.

27:55.424 --> 27:58.802
Mi-ji, I've just done something
very stupid!

27:59.344 --> 28:02.556
I got on the wrong bus
and ended up very far from home.

28:03.307 --> 28:05.601
So I won't be able to get home today.

28:07.102 --> 28:08.687
Hey, Ho-su.

28:14.443 --> 28:16.153
What are you doing over there?

28:18.530 --> 28:20.240
Your mom called.

28:21.366 --> 28:24.536
She said she got on the wrong bus,
so she can't come home today.

28:26.538 --> 28:27.581
What?

28:28.081 --> 28:30.792
She said she'll catch
the first bus back tomorrow.

28:30.876 --> 28:32.878
She said to lock up before going to bed.

28:46.808 --> 28:49.770
Ho-su! Why are you crying?

28:55.525 --> 28:56.693
Don't cry.

29:03.575 --> 29:06.078
Why did you cry that day?

29:06.161 --> 29:08.622
I got so flustered
that I couldn't even ask you.

29:08.705 --> 29:10.624
I thought my mom had abandoned me.

29:10.707 --> 29:13.377
Hey, how could your mom abandon you?

29:14.211 --> 29:15.671
Back then, I thought she did.

29:18.423 --> 29:22.177
I was sitting in the living room
with the table set for the ancestral rite,

29:22.261 --> 29:24.221
and it felt so quiet.

29:25.222 --> 29:27.849
In that silence,
all I could hear was my own breath.

29:29.184 --> 29:32.396
I felt like I was alone in the universe.

29:33.814 --> 29:36.733
Since that day,
I've been preparing little by little.

29:36.817 --> 29:40.946
If my mom ever gets on the wrong bus again
and wants to go far away,

29:41.530 --> 29:43.282
I don't want to be a burden to her.

29:43.824 --> 29:45.826
In my own way, I'm just preparing myself

29:46.743 --> 29:49.538
so I don't break down
if I end up alone again like that day.

29:49.621 --> 29:53.166
You weren't alone that day.

29:53.250 --> 29:56.336
I waited by your side
until you stopped crying.

29:56.420 --> 29:57.546
You're right.

29:59.047 --> 30:02.050
You had no idea what was going on,
but you cried with me.

30:03.969 --> 30:05.387
Looking back now,

30:06.305 --> 30:08.640
I think it was like that every time.

30:09.516 --> 30:11.643
Whenever I started thinking
about why life was so quiet,

30:11.727 --> 30:14.980
you would barge in, loud as ever.

30:15.063 --> 30:17.357
What? "Loud as ever"?

30:17.441 --> 30:19.651
If you don't like that,
maybe I should leave.

30:19.735 --> 30:22.321
- No. I like that you're loud.
- Gosh.

30:36.710 --> 30:38.879
What? No?

30:38.962 --> 30:41.631
- Like this? No…
- I think it's better to sit. Here…

30:42.591 --> 30:44.217
Wait…

30:44.301 --> 30:46.470
- Oh, my alarm!
- Why is the alarm…

30:46.553 --> 30:47.929
Why is this…

30:48.638 --> 30:50.098
going off now?

30:50.182 --> 30:54.186
Probably because it's the weekend.
It's better to sleep in.

30:55.062 --> 30:57.105
Wait. No way.

30:57.981 --> 31:00.025
Wow! Unbelievable.

31:00.108 --> 31:01.860
You still have this?

31:04.654 --> 31:08.784
You wrote in the guidebook
as if you were studying for a test.

31:09.409 --> 31:11.495
You told me to check
where we should go together.

31:13.955 --> 31:16.666
Hey, should we follow the guidebook?

31:16.750 --> 31:18.001
Right now?

31:21.088 --> 31:22.756
There we go. Hold this.

31:23.465 --> 31:24.424
This?

31:26.551 --> 31:27.969
Wait for me.

31:39.064 --> 31:40.315
There it is!

32:14.349 --> 32:18.770
CLOSED TODAY DUE TO PERSONAL REASONS

32:18.854 --> 32:21.481
SEOUL'S HIDDEN GEMS
MI-JI & HO-SU'S SEOUL TRIP

32:23.275 --> 32:25.527
Somehow, we ended up near your office.

32:26.611 --> 32:29.531
Do you want to go somewhere else?
I'm sorry we ended up here.

32:30.157 --> 32:31.867
No, I wanted to come here.

32:34.286 --> 32:36.496
This guidebook is a complete joke.

32:36.580 --> 32:38.915
Why don't the places
I wanted to visit exist anymore?

32:38.999 --> 32:40.959
Well, the book is over ten years old.

32:41.042 --> 32:42.794
I should've looked them up first.

32:42.878 --> 32:44.838
I'm sorry for dragging you around.

32:44.921 --> 32:47.299
Don't be sorry. I had fun.

32:57.684 --> 33:00.395
He's quiet. Is he tired?

33:00.937 --> 33:03.607
Or maybe he's bored
of hanging around with me.

33:04.149 --> 33:07.277
Or is he upset
because I kept dragging him around?

33:09.279 --> 33:12.449
Should we just head home
after we finish eating this?

33:13.700 --> 33:14.618
Why?

33:14.701 --> 33:17.078
I feel like today's not our day.

33:17.162 --> 33:20.749
People always end up getting hurt
or fighting on an unlucky day like this.

33:20.832 --> 33:24.920
After this, let's go somewhere
that's definitely still there.

33:25.003 --> 33:28.215
It's not like Namsan or Gyeongbokgung
Palace could have disappeared, right?

33:28.298 --> 33:30.133
There's an art museum nearby too.

33:30.217 --> 33:32.761
No, let's go another time.

33:35.013 --> 33:37.891
Why? Is it because of me?

33:37.974 --> 33:40.852
No, it's not because of you.

33:41.853 --> 33:47.609
I'm just realizing
that ten years is a really long time.

33:48.443 --> 33:51.988
Everything's changed so much.
I feel so behind.

33:55.283 --> 33:56.368
Let's buy a new one.

33:57.035 --> 33:58.620
- A new what?
- A guidebook.

33:59.496 --> 34:01.331
I'll buy this year's edition

34:01.414 --> 34:03.124
and study it again.

34:05.502 --> 34:06.962
Let's go right now.

34:08.630 --> 34:09.631
Okay.

34:12.592 --> 34:13.552
Ho-su!

34:14.636 --> 34:16.805
My gosh, Mr. Lee.

34:16.888 --> 34:19.099
What brings you two here?

34:19.182 --> 34:22.060
We have a trial tomorrow,
so we have to work this weekend.

34:24.104 --> 34:27.190
Is this the crochet lady
you were talking about?

34:27.941 --> 34:30.318
- Yes, she is…
- My goodness!

34:30.402 --> 34:32.487
Mr. Lee has told me so much about you.

34:32.571 --> 34:33.446
Hello.

34:33.530 --> 34:35.824
Who is she again?

34:36.950 --> 34:39.244
- We were classmates--
- She's my girlfriend.

34:39.327 --> 34:41.413
You're his girlfriend.

34:43.456 --> 34:46.251
You were classmates?
So you went to our university?

34:46.334 --> 34:48.420
No, we were high school classmates.

34:49.212 --> 34:52.048
I see. Then…

34:53.091 --> 34:54.509
are you a lawyer?

34:55.302 --> 34:56.761
Why are you asking that?

34:56.845 --> 34:58.346
I work at a public corporation.

34:58.430 --> 35:00.932
It's a finance management
corporation near here.

35:01.016 --> 35:04.144
- I see.
- Yes.

35:09.983 --> 35:11.318
The travel section's here.

35:20.577 --> 35:21.453
What?

35:22.662 --> 35:23.997
Why did you do that earlier?

35:27.000 --> 35:28.084
Do what?

35:28.835 --> 35:30.086
You pretended to be Mi-rae.

35:31.880 --> 35:34.591
They don't even know you,
so why did you…

35:35.216 --> 35:37.385
I didn't want to put you
in an awkward position.

35:37.469 --> 35:39.554
Why would I be in an awkward position?

35:40.930 --> 35:42.766
Then what was I supposed to say?

35:42.849 --> 35:46.144
You told them I was your girlfriend.
Was I supposed to say I'm unemployed?

35:47.103 --> 35:48.563
I wouldn't have minded.

35:49.606 --> 35:53.652
Well, they were obviously
your former coworkers.

35:54.694 --> 35:57.030
I didn't want to embarrass you.

35:57.530 --> 36:00.450
So you lied because of me?

36:01.242 --> 36:03.578
That's not what I meant.

36:04.204 --> 36:05.497
Let's head back.

36:06.665 --> 36:07.957
What?

36:08.041 --> 36:10.210
You were right.
Today doesn't seem to be our day.

36:19.803 --> 36:21.346
All right.

36:33.900 --> 36:36.903
TO MI-RAE

36:42.575 --> 36:44.202
Speak of the devil.

36:48.331 --> 36:49.541
Director Yoon.

36:49.624 --> 36:50.625
How have you been?

37:21.656 --> 37:23.491
Why do things keep going sideways?

37:24.200 --> 37:26.661
Is it because I'm a puzzle piece
that doesn't fit?

37:29.122 --> 37:31.791
No matter how much I pretend to be normal,

37:31.875 --> 37:33.960
I'm still broken. Will I ever be able…

37:35.420 --> 37:37.422
to form a pair with someone else?

37:38.673 --> 37:40.425
Today really isn't my day.

37:48.433 --> 37:49.726
One, two, three.

37:50.810 --> 37:51.978
There we go.

38:04.699 --> 38:06.451
He took more of his things.

38:20.340 --> 38:21.341
Bun-hong.

38:26.012 --> 38:28.139
Come with us. You even got flowers.

38:28.223 --> 38:29.974
I know there's no urgent business--

38:31.017 --> 38:33.269
You two should go alone.

38:33.353 --> 38:34.604
I think that'll be best.

38:34.687 --> 38:37.357
We can't just go without you.
We're a family.

38:37.440 --> 38:38.775
Why not?

38:38.858 --> 38:42.362
One day, I'll be the one ditching you
to hang out with just Ho-su.

38:44.489 --> 38:47.367
I guess this is why everyone
was so against this marriage.

38:48.159 --> 38:51.579
I even promised
that you would never feel lonely again,

38:51.663 --> 38:54.165
but Ho-su won't listen to me these days.

38:54.249 --> 38:56.835
Honey, I told you…

38:57.836 --> 38:59.420
that I was the oddball in my family.

39:00.421 --> 39:02.090
Feeling alone within a family

39:02.173 --> 39:04.551
is lonelier than
being alone anywhere else.

39:05.093 --> 39:07.971
It makes you feel sad and small.

39:09.264 --> 39:12.725
What I'm most worried about
is that our Ho-su will feel that way too.

39:13.852 --> 39:16.020
Let's not make Ho-su feel lonely.

39:22.402 --> 39:24.779
I'll be back soon.

39:26.155 --> 39:28.199
It's not like he's even healthy.

39:28.283 --> 39:31.494
You'll have to take care of him
his whole life.

39:31.578 --> 39:34.372
Why take on that burden?

39:35.582 --> 39:39.002
Since when did you two worry about me?

39:39.085 --> 39:40.044
What?

39:42.130 --> 39:43.464
You two…

39:44.465 --> 39:46.009
Our family…

39:48.261 --> 39:50.471
When did you ever care about me?

39:52.056 --> 39:53.766
You're just embarrassed.

39:54.934 --> 39:57.020
You said you were embarrassed
to call me family

39:57.103 --> 40:01.816
because I didn't have a decent job
and got married late to a man with a kid.

40:01.900 --> 40:03.526
Hey!

40:03.610 --> 40:05.737
We said those things for your sake!

40:07.572 --> 40:08.781
For my sake?

40:11.618 --> 40:12.994
You should go now.

40:13.494 --> 40:14.662
Bun-hong.

40:14.746 --> 40:17.206
If you decide to raise him,
then you're no longer family.

40:17.290 --> 40:18.875
Choose. Him or us?

40:18.958 --> 40:20.043
Don't you know?

40:20.668 --> 40:22.337
I chose a long time ago.

40:24.422 --> 40:28.176
Are you really going to cut ties with us
for that brat who's not even yours?

40:29.552 --> 40:30.929
What did you say?

40:32.764 --> 40:33.890
"That brat"?

40:34.933 --> 40:36.059
"That brat"?

40:37.435 --> 40:39.562
Who are you to call him that?

40:40.271 --> 40:41.606
He's my son.

40:42.440 --> 40:45.610
You have no right to call my son that!

40:46.235 --> 40:49.948
Your mom and I went
to the same high school.

40:50.031 --> 40:52.075
Nice to meet you.

40:55.495 --> 40:58.623
- It's so good to see you. Gosh!
- Yes, it is.

40:58.706 --> 41:01.501
He's a bit quiet.

41:01.584 --> 41:02.543
Yes.

41:03.753 --> 41:05.254
He takes after me.

41:05.338 --> 41:07.340
He's always been a little shy.

41:07.423 --> 41:10.551
I wish he had taken after his late dad
in that regard.

41:11.052 --> 41:12.720
But he's just like me.

41:13.388 --> 41:15.098
Why are you doing all this?

41:15.181 --> 41:17.934
You don't have to pretend
we're family when nobody is around.

41:18.017 --> 41:19.727
I…

41:21.229 --> 41:23.314
I was just doing it for you--

41:23.398 --> 41:24.774
If you care about me…

41:25.525 --> 41:27.151
then just ignore me.

41:48.548 --> 41:50.425
An-na, it's been ages!

41:53.928 --> 41:56.764
What do you mean?
Who's in critical condition?

41:56.848 --> 41:59.976
Your sisters didn't tell you
that your mother is sick?

42:00.059 --> 42:04.689
I know they cut ties with you,
but how could they not tell you?

42:14.991 --> 42:17.910
Hey, it's me! Where's Mom?

42:18.411 --> 42:20.955
Which hospital is she in?
I'll go there right now.

42:21.748 --> 42:23.541
Don't come. Mom is fine now.

42:24.584 --> 42:25.877
Where is she?

42:26.627 --> 42:29.464
You should've told me
that Mom was in critical condition.

42:30.298 --> 42:32.300
You're not even family. Why do you care?

42:33.384 --> 42:34.635
What?

42:34.719 --> 42:37.764
How dare you call me
after cutting ties with us and leaving?

42:37.847 --> 42:39.724
This is a family matter,
so we'll handle it.

42:39.807 --> 42:41.684
Mind your own business.

42:42.727 --> 42:43.811
Wait.

42:45.104 --> 42:46.105
Hey!

42:56.115 --> 42:58.826
One ticket for Duson Terminal, please.

42:59.911 --> 43:01.746
There are no tickets for that destination.

43:01.829 --> 43:02.955
The last bus just left.

43:03.039 --> 43:04.499
What?

43:42.662 --> 43:43.746
Hi.

43:44.872 --> 43:46.582
It's me, Bun-hong.

43:47.625 --> 43:49.168
Are you Mi-ji or Mi-rae?

43:50.670 --> 43:52.171
Mi-ji.

43:58.594 --> 44:00.179
I…

44:01.472 --> 44:03.474
I've just done something very stupid!

44:04.016 --> 44:06.853
I got on the wrong bus
and ended up very far from home.

44:07.937 --> 44:10.398
So I won't be able to get home today.

44:11.566 --> 44:13.776
Please tell Ho-su that tomorrow morning…

44:14.360 --> 44:17.363
I'll get the first bus back home.

44:18.156 --> 44:20.783
So could you tell him to lock up
before going to bed?

44:26.164 --> 44:27.498
The truth is,

44:27.582 --> 44:30.543
I had a small fight with Ho-su today.

44:32.420 --> 44:34.172
Don't tell him that I told you.

44:36.257 --> 44:38.593
Yes, thank you.

45:22.637 --> 45:24.972
- We were classmates--
- She's my girlfriend.

45:25.056 --> 45:28.017
So you lied because of me?

45:29.435 --> 45:32.188
That's not what I meant.

45:32.271 --> 45:33.648
Let's head back.

45:34.315 --> 45:37.193
Jeez! Am I a compulsive liar or something?

45:37.276 --> 45:39.445
Why did I lie about that?

45:41.864 --> 45:44.116
This must be a new record.

45:44.200 --> 45:48.371
How could I disappoint him as soon
as he introduced me as his girlfriend?

45:50.248 --> 45:53.501
Why is nothing working out today?

45:55.920 --> 45:58.256
MR. PARK SANG-YEONG

46:02.677 --> 46:05.388
MR. PARK SANG-YEONG

46:08.099 --> 46:09.809
Why is he suddenly calling me?

46:10.810 --> 46:15.167
MI-RAE! I LOVE YOU!

46:17.483 --> 46:20.027
Why did that jerk call out of the blue?

46:20.111 --> 46:21.779
Is he really returning soon?

46:22.697 --> 46:25.449
I need to back out of
this new HQ project before he does.

46:25.533 --> 46:26.617
CONFIDENTIAL

46:26.701 --> 46:28.869
How do I do that
without getting in trouble?

46:44.093 --> 46:46.429
Excuse me, sir.

46:46.512 --> 46:47.805
Hello.

46:47.888 --> 46:49.223
Mr. Park!

46:49.307 --> 46:50.975
Hey, you're back!

46:51.058 --> 46:52.518
Sang-yeong!

46:52.601 --> 46:54.353
- Oh my.
- Oh my gosh!

46:55.271 --> 46:56.647
You're back already?

46:56.731 --> 46:58.524
- Welcome back.
- How have you been?

46:58.607 --> 47:01.193
- You look great.
- Oh, come on. I'm still…

47:01.277 --> 47:02.778
You look good.

47:02.862 --> 47:05.614
- How have you been?
- That guy is Park Sang-yeong?

47:05.698 --> 47:08.117
- How have you been?
- How was it?

47:26.427 --> 47:28.637
- How have you been?
- Well, I…

47:40.816 --> 47:42.193
How have you been?

47:58.959 --> 48:00.586
If you were to meet…

48:01.420 --> 48:04.256
someone who looks just like Dad,

48:04.882 --> 48:06.592
how do you think you'd feel?

48:07.718 --> 48:10.137
Dad? That's a random question.

48:11.514 --> 48:12.723
Well…

48:14.558 --> 48:15.935
I think I'd be surprised,

48:16.769 --> 48:18.270
and then I'd feel happy.

48:18.813 --> 48:21.899
I would want to talk to him
and spend time with him.

48:22.608 --> 48:24.235
Even if he's not our dad…

48:25.152 --> 48:26.821
and he just looks like him?

48:27.530 --> 48:31.409
I'd know that in my head,
but I think I'd still be drawn to him.

48:32.618 --> 48:35.121
What about you?
How do you think you'd feel?

48:37.415 --> 48:40.042
I would hope that he's a good person,

48:40.668 --> 48:41.877
like our dad.

49:13.451 --> 49:17.705
MI-JI

49:26.380 --> 49:28.924
One, two, three. My goodness.

49:31.177 --> 49:36.432
I used to fold your thermals
like that, you know.

49:42.897 --> 49:46.066
Grandma, I'm going back to Seoul now.

49:46.150 --> 49:48.360
Will you come back soon?

49:50.279 --> 49:52.740
Or are you going to stay in Seoul?

49:53.574 --> 49:54.575
I don't know.

49:54.658 --> 49:56.327
Why don't you know?

49:57.286 --> 49:58.954
You're the one making the decision.

50:00.414 --> 50:01.874
Grandma…

50:03.876 --> 50:05.127
If I decide…

50:05.878 --> 50:07.838
to stay here like I am right now,

50:09.006 --> 50:10.382
would it be too pathetic?

50:11.467 --> 50:14.386
If I say no,

50:15.262 --> 50:16.847
won't it be pathetic?

50:18.599 --> 50:21.602
You're right. I just feel pathetic.

50:25.147 --> 50:27.274
I feel like I keep making
the same mistake.

50:28.192 --> 50:29.360
Mistake?

50:29.860 --> 50:31.987
I shouldn't be relying on someone

50:32.071 --> 50:34.865
just because I'm having
a tough time right now.

50:36.867 --> 50:38.827
I already went through this before.

50:40.621 --> 50:42.623
But I keep wanting to trust that person.

50:44.625 --> 50:46.377
I feel so pathetic.

50:48.921 --> 50:50.005
I feel…

50:50.798 --> 50:53.133
very pathetic too.

50:54.051 --> 50:56.720
I can't even use the restroom by myself.

50:57.555 --> 51:00.057
Grandma, you can't help that, though.

51:01.100 --> 51:03.811
You can't help how you feel either.

51:06.313 --> 51:09.775
Don't call yourself pathetic.

51:37.886 --> 51:39.638
Ma'am, I'm here.

51:45.102 --> 51:46.770
Can we get more water here?

51:46.854 --> 51:47.813
Okay.

51:53.193 --> 51:55.487
Hyeon Sang-wol. You know her, right?

51:56.280 --> 51:59.116
Why are you bringing up
a dead person's name out of the blue?

51:59.199 --> 52:02.077
I heard you two were like family
up until she died.

52:02.161 --> 52:06.373
You're even talking to me
just because I mentioned her name.

52:10.169 --> 52:13.756
Sell your restaurant to KFMC.

52:14.548 --> 52:16.759
Then you'll never have to see me

52:16.842 --> 52:20.554
or hear the name Hyeon Sang-wol again.

52:21.472 --> 52:25.643
I already declined
through my legal representative.

52:25.726 --> 52:27.811
Did Ho-su tell you
that everything was settled?

52:33.317 --> 52:34.902
Do you two know each other?

52:34.985 --> 52:36.362
He didn't tell you?

52:38.447 --> 52:41.700
He was my favorite junior colleague.

52:41.784 --> 52:43.369
Enjoy your meal.

52:46.330 --> 52:48.999
Ma'am, you said you had a favor to ask.

52:50.459 --> 52:52.544
Should I come back later if you're busy?

52:52.628 --> 52:55.506
You don't have to. I figured it out.

52:55.589 --> 52:56.757
Pardon?

52:57.925 --> 52:59.927
What was it about?

53:00.010 --> 53:01.887
You don't need to worry about that.

53:02.638 --> 53:03.806
You can go now.

53:16.944 --> 53:18.112
Ms. Yu.

53:22.366 --> 53:24.368
I'm sorry if I startled you.

53:25.452 --> 53:28.414
You seemed uncomfortable inside
because of the other people.

53:31.166 --> 53:32.084
Why…

53:33.836 --> 53:37.005
Can I talk to you in private at lunch?

53:37.798 --> 53:39.007
It won't take long.

53:50.269 --> 53:53.230
So what did you want to talk about?

53:54.148 --> 54:00.404
I heard earlier that you were in charge
of the new HQ project.

54:01.447 --> 54:02.322
Is it true?

54:03.031 --> 54:04.658
Yes, so what?

54:05.284 --> 54:08.495
I was actually in charge of that project.

54:09.329 --> 54:11.415
So before I officially
start working again,

54:12.040 --> 54:14.418
I thought it'd be better
if we sorted things out first.

54:15.878 --> 54:20.215
To be honest, I was a bit surprised
when I heard you volunteered for it.

54:20.841 --> 54:23.886
Are you saying that I can't work on it
because it was your project?

54:23.969 --> 54:26.764
No, Ms. Yu. That's not what I meant.

54:29.433 --> 54:33.937
You already know this,
but everyone steers clear of that project.

54:34.605 --> 54:38.150
People feel uncomfortable because
it's a task force led by the director.

54:38.233 --> 54:39.902
And if things don't go well,

54:39.985 --> 54:43.197
there's a chance that someone
on the very bottom would be blamed.

54:43.280 --> 54:44.448
Just like Su-yeon.

54:45.324 --> 54:47.326
That's why I decided to volunteer for it,

54:47.409 --> 54:49.745
so when I heard you took over,
I was surprised.

54:49.828 --> 54:52.206
I didn't mean it like that.
Don't get the wrong idea.

54:52.998 --> 54:55.959
So how did you want to sort things out?

54:56.043 --> 54:57.294
I think…

54:58.337 --> 55:01.882
it's best if one of us
stops working on the project.

55:01.965 --> 55:04.426
It'll give people less reason to gossip.

55:04.510 --> 55:05.969
You want me to step down?

55:06.053 --> 55:08.055
If I back out right now,

55:08.138 --> 55:10.307
the company will find a way
to use that against me.

55:10.390 --> 55:12.434
I can back out.

55:13.769 --> 55:15.729
- Pardon?
- I heard that…

55:16.271 --> 55:18.440
you worked very hard on it
while I was away.

55:19.191 --> 55:21.193
It sounds like you made
a lot of progress too.

55:21.276 --> 55:25.364
If you're willing to take the risk
and see this through…

55:27.199 --> 55:28.951
then I'll back out.

55:29.034 --> 55:30.911
But if you're not backing out

55:30.994 --> 55:33.872
because you're worried
about the repercussions,

55:33.956 --> 55:36.542
then I can take care of that for you.

55:37.251 --> 55:41.088
Either way, I'll make sure
you're not put in a difficult position.

55:41.964 --> 55:43.423
Do whatever you want to do.

55:44.591 --> 55:47.594
Why would you go that far for me?

55:49.888 --> 55:51.390
You mentioned before…

55:52.307 --> 55:56.144
that I look a lot like your late father.

55:57.729 --> 56:01.316
You said you still miss him sometimes
because he was such a good person.

56:02.109 --> 56:05.279
That's probably why you trusted me
so much and relied on me.

56:06.572 --> 56:09.575
But I feel like I didn't live up
to your expectations.

56:09.658 --> 56:10.909
I feel bad about that.

56:15.539 --> 56:17.916
I'll back out.

56:18.792 --> 56:23.005
But in exchange, please make sure
that I don't get penalized in any way.

56:23.630 --> 56:26.216
Okay. I will.

56:29.553 --> 56:33.223
I have something to give you.
It's not much, but…

56:43.442 --> 56:44.651
It's a bookmark.

56:45.360 --> 56:47.070
Mi-rae helped me pick it out yesterday.

56:48.030 --> 56:51.533
I don't know if you'll like it.
It's what Mi-rae liked.

56:51.617 --> 56:54.202
What are you talking about? When did I…

56:54.953 --> 56:58.332
I'm sorry.
That must've sounded confusing.

56:58.874 --> 57:00.918
I was talking about my Mi-rae.

57:04.254 --> 57:05.505
My daughter.

57:08.383 --> 57:11.219
Gosh, Mi-rae has grown so much
in a short period of time.

57:12.262 --> 57:14.890
I've heard that other kids
always ask for their moms,

57:15.849 --> 57:17.643
but she's such a Daddy's girl.

57:18.310 --> 57:22.022
She's always asking for me
when she's playing or sleeping.

57:23.732 --> 57:24.858
Mi-ji.

57:31.990 --> 57:35.243
Knock, knock. Can I come in?

57:40.749 --> 57:41.959
Goodness.

57:42.793 --> 57:43.877
Mi-ji.

57:44.419 --> 57:46.296
Why are you pouting?

57:47.172 --> 57:48.757
Do you want to give me a kiss?

57:50.926 --> 57:54.429
Gosh, you're not even looking at me.

57:55.430 --> 57:58.475
I guess I should just
go see Mi-rae at the hospital again.

58:02.771 --> 58:04.856
Okay. I'm sorry.

58:04.940 --> 58:07.901
Gosh, I'm sorry. I was just kidding.

58:09.653 --> 58:10.862
Goodness.

58:11.405 --> 58:14.241
What made you so upset and sad, Mi-ji?

58:14.992 --> 58:18.578
You and Mom only like Mi-rae.

58:18.662 --> 58:22.332
I wish I was sick too.

58:25.711 --> 58:27.337
You're jealous of Mi-rae?

58:31.717 --> 58:32.801
Mi-ji.

58:33.677 --> 58:36.013
Can I tell you a secret?

58:38.724 --> 58:42.352
Mi-rae said she envies you
more than anyone else in the world.

58:42.853 --> 58:43.895
Why?

58:44.438 --> 58:48.108
Because you can hold your breath
underwater for more than a minute.

58:48.191 --> 58:51.653
Plus, you can drink whole milk.
You can even do a handstand too.

58:51.737 --> 58:54.698
Mi-rae cried
and said that she wants to be like you.

58:57.993 --> 58:59.953
Sweetie, give me your hand.

59:01.455 --> 59:06.460
Mi-rae collected
all the sky blue ones for you.

59:07.294 --> 59:09.004
She wouldn't give me a single one.

59:11.548 --> 59:12.716
Mi-ji.

59:13.759 --> 59:15.385
Even when I'm not with you,

59:15.969 --> 59:20.807
you and Mi-rae
are still both my favorites, okay?

59:49.503 --> 59:52.130
MI-RAE

59:53.840 --> 59:55.050
Hello.

59:55.550 --> 59:57.094
What are you doing?

59:57.177 --> 59:59.638
Are you getting ready to come back?

01:00:00.222 --> 01:00:02.474
Yes. Why?

01:00:02.557 --> 01:00:04.184
Has something happened at the office?

01:00:05.977 --> 01:00:08.063
No, I'm just calling.

01:00:09.147 --> 01:00:11.608
I was just curious
if you were wrapping things up.

01:00:12.484 --> 01:00:14.569
Have you decided what to do?

01:00:16.279 --> 01:00:18.573
No, I haven't fully decided yet,

01:00:19.241 --> 01:00:20.992
but I have an idea.

01:00:21.701 --> 01:00:22.744
What is it?

01:00:23.245 --> 01:00:26.581
I'll tell you later.
It's too early to tell you.

01:00:26.665 --> 01:00:29.042
Then who would you talk to about it?

01:00:30.710 --> 01:00:33.547
Is it something you would have
spoken to Dad about?

01:00:33.630 --> 01:00:34.673
What?

01:00:35.340 --> 01:00:36.842
I met Park Sang-yeong.

01:00:41.763 --> 01:00:42.848
Mi-ji…

01:00:43.431 --> 01:00:45.851
I don't know what he told you, but…

01:00:45.934 --> 01:00:47.144
Mi-rae.

01:00:47.227 --> 01:00:51.231
I don't care about what he says
or what the rumor says.

01:00:51.314 --> 01:00:55.485
What I want to know
is your side of the story, Mi-rae.

01:00:55.986 --> 01:00:59.197
Even if you can't tell anyone else,
you can be honest with me.

01:00:59.281 --> 01:01:01.408
So why aren't you telling me? Why?

01:01:01.491 --> 01:01:03.076
Because no one believes me.

01:01:04.452 --> 01:01:08.248
No matter how much I insisted
that it isn't true, no one believed me.

01:01:09.541 --> 01:01:12.085
But if you don't believe me either,
then I really…

01:01:13.378 --> 01:01:14.713
But I know.

01:01:15.797 --> 01:01:18.508
No one else in the world
may understand you,

01:01:18.592 --> 01:01:20.802
but I know it's because of Dad.

01:01:22.721 --> 01:01:24.598
I told myself I'd spit

01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:27.809
in the face of that darn Park Sang-yeong
if I ever met him.

01:01:27.893 --> 01:01:29.644
But when I finally saw him…

01:01:30.604 --> 01:01:33.481
I started tearing up.

01:01:35.233 --> 01:01:37.402
I knew he wasn't our dad,

01:01:38.403 --> 01:01:41.448
but I couldn't even talk right,
like an idiot.

01:01:41.531 --> 01:01:43.658
You must've felt the same way, Mi-rae.

01:01:44.910 --> 01:01:48.121
So why didn't you tell me, you idiot?

01:01:49.164 --> 01:01:50.790
Because I felt like a fool.

01:01:52.375 --> 01:01:54.586
I feel so stupid for letting…

01:01:56.004 --> 01:01:58.173
someone like him remind me of Dad

01:01:59.507 --> 01:02:01.509
and for wanting him to be a good person.

01:02:02.844 --> 01:02:04.221
You're so…

01:02:05.138 --> 01:02:07.390
What is wrong with us?

01:02:08.892 --> 01:02:12.562
We couldn't even tell each other
that we missed Dad,

01:02:12.646 --> 01:02:16.066
so we ended up…

01:02:37.379 --> 01:02:39.965
Mi-ji. Yesterday, I…

01:02:46.388 --> 01:02:48.974
Are you free tomorrow?

01:02:59.150 --> 01:03:01.236
I'm… sorry.

01:03:02.529 --> 01:03:04.489
Your cellphone
is practically attached to you

01:03:04.572 --> 01:03:06.533
now that you're in a relationship.

01:03:06.616 --> 01:03:07.575
No, I…

01:03:08.451 --> 01:03:10.996
So, why did you want to see me so late?

01:03:11.079 --> 01:03:14.958
You said you were helping someone
last time. Are you done with that?

01:03:15.041 --> 01:03:17.961
If you are,
then you should go for an interview.

01:03:18.044 --> 01:03:19.754
You know A&A, right?

01:03:20.380 --> 01:03:23.300
It's not one of the top three firms,
but it's a decent one.

01:03:23.383 --> 01:03:26.761
Gosh, it's not just decent.
It's a great place.

01:03:27.971 --> 01:03:29.014
But…

01:03:30.098 --> 01:03:32.309
Mr. Lee has probably
already spoken to them about me…

01:03:32.392 --> 01:03:33.393
Mr. Lee.

01:03:33.476 --> 01:03:36.021
He's not the only one
with connections, you know?

01:03:36.104 --> 01:03:37.731
I have them too.

01:03:38.648 --> 01:03:41.693
The lawyer I worked for
as a newbie is a partner there.

01:03:42.193 --> 01:03:45.572
I've already told them about you,
so you should go for an interview.

01:03:46.406 --> 01:03:49.534
Did you also tell them
how I ended up quitting?

01:03:49.617 --> 01:03:53.163
Gosh, I recommended you,
so they won't even care about that!

01:03:57.751 --> 01:03:59.252
Let's go eat.

01:04:12.474 --> 01:04:14.017
SENIOR SPECIALIST YU MI-RAE

01:04:14.100 --> 01:04:15.977
I'm ready now.

01:04:16.644 --> 01:04:18.938
So I'll take care of the rest myself
when I'm back.

01:04:19.022 --> 01:04:20.440
Don't worry.

01:04:25.653 --> 01:04:27.197
Why aren't you eating lunch?

01:04:27.280 --> 01:04:30.325
I'm just organizing my desk.

01:04:31.493 --> 01:04:33.995
You looked like you were having
a hard time yesterday.

01:04:35.538 --> 01:04:38.958
Will you be okay handling
the new HQ project with Mr. Park back?

01:04:39.042 --> 01:04:41.002
I backed out of that.

01:04:42.003 --> 01:04:44.672
- Pardon?
- Even without Mr. Park,

01:04:44.756 --> 01:04:46.549
I would've dropped the project anyway.

01:04:46.633 --> 01:04:48.718
Why, though?

01:04:49.552 --> 01:04:51.179
You worked so hard on it.

01:04:51.262 --> 01:04:54.808
I don't know how much longer
I'll keep working here,

01:04:54.891 --> 01:04:57.685
so I don't see the point
in working so hard.

01:04:58.603 --> 01:05:01.648
Starting next week,
I'm going to live a little differently.

01:05:02.273 --> 01:05:04.692
So don't be surprised
if I act like someone else.

01:05:07.487 --> 01:05:09.406
I mean, I'm totally fine.

01:05:14.160 --> 01:05:16.287
Thank you for being so nice to me, Tae-i.

01:05:17.789 --> 01:05:18.915
From now on…

01:05:20.250 --> 01:05:23.044
please be even nicer to me.

01:05:35.765 --> 01:05:36.724
HO-SU

01:05:36.808 --> 01:05:39.477
Do you have time after work today?

01:05:42.063 --> 01:05:44.774
You look awful. My gosh.

01:05:44.858 --> 01:05:46.025
Step aside.

01:05:49.779 --> 01:05:52.157
What is it? What do you want?

01:05:53.908 --> 01:05:56.161
I came to help you wash your greasy hair.

01:05:56.244 --> 01:05:57.537
Got a problem?

01:05:57.620 --> 01:06:01.040
Gosh, that's okay.
I can go to a hair salon.

01:06:01.124 --> 01:06:02.709
Like hell you will.

01:06:02.792 --> 01:06:05.795
As if you'd go to a hair salon
looking like that.

01:06:07.964 --> 01:06:09.257
Come on. Hurry up.

01:06:11.509 --> 01:06:13.386
What's the point of having a great son?

01:06:14.262 --> 01:06:16.681
You don't have anyone
to help you wash your hair.

01:06:17.223 --> 01:06:20.602
Why did Ho-su go back so soon
when he doesn't even work now?

01:06:20.685 --> 01:06:24.772
I told him to hurry up and go back.

01:06:25.273 --> 01:06:27.901
I didn't want him
to see me looking like a mess.

01:06:28.860 --> 01:06:30.737
Jeez, you're not dating him.

01:06:32.071 --> 01:06:33.781
Why are you shy around your own son?

01:06:33.865 --> 01:06:36.576
Sometimes, when I look at you two,

01:06:36.659 --> 01:06:39.537
I feel like I'm watching
an educational show instead of a family.

01:06:39.621 --> 01:06:42.332
You're always so polite
and proper to each other.

01:06:42.415 --> 01:06:44.250
Even actors don't act like that.

01:06:48.421 --> 01:06:49.923
What I'm saying is…

01:06:50.673 --> 01:06:53.009
Ho-su isn't like other kids his age.

01:06:53.092 --> 01:06:54.719
He's so calm and collected.

01:06:55.595 --> 01:06:58.097
Was Ho-su's dad that quiet?

01:06:58.181 --> 01:07:01.017
No, Ho-su's mom was.

01:07:01.100 --> 01:07:02.477
Jeez.

01:07:03.102 --> 01:07:05.688
Quiet? The chaotic Yeom Bun-hong?

01:07:05.772 --> 01:07:08.691
He's not like you at all.

01:07:08.775 --> 01:07:10.068
You're being ridiculous.

01:07:10.151 --> 01:07:11.611
Not me.

01:07:12.153 --> 01:07:13.613
Ho-su's biological mom.

01:07:16.491 --> 01:07:17.367
Hey.

01:07:18.535 --> 01:07:19.994
What are you talking about?

01:07:20.954 --> 01:07:23.831
I'm not Ho-su's mom.

01:07:24.415 --> 01:07:26.376
Ho-su's dad remarried.

01:07:28.545 --> 01:07:30.088
I knew it.

01:07:31.089 --> 01:07:33.466
I knew you were sharp.

01:07:34.634 --> 01:07:37.053
I tried acting like a mom,

01:07:37.136 --> 01:07:39.097
but I never knew how to.

01:07:39.764 --> 01:07:42.934
No matter how hard I tried,
I was just a poor imitation.

01:07:43.017 --> 01:07:45.645
We probably never even seemed
like a real family.

01:07:45.728 --> 01:07:47.063
My gosh.

01:07:51.526 --> 01:07:52.527
Hey.

01:07:53.152 --> 01:07:55.238
You don't have to give birth to be a mom.

01:07:55.989 --> 01:07:57.574
You just give them your DNA.

01:07:57.657 --> 01:08:00.827
There are so many people
who don't deserve to be parents.

01:08:00.910 --> 01:08:03.246
Giving birth doesn't
automatically make you a mom.

01:08:03.329 --> 01:08:04.831
Take me, for example.

01:08:04.914 --> 01:08:07.834
I gave birth to two kids,
but I can't even tell them apart.

01:08:12.297 --> 01:08:14.799
I saw how you raised your son.

01:08:15.466 --> 01:08:16.718
An "imitation"?

01:08:17.260 --> 01:08:21.014
You think you can raise a kid
the way you did by imitating other moms?

01:08:21.097 --> 01:08:22.098
Bun-hong.

01:08:23.057 --> 01:08:25.101
You raised Ho-su all by yourself.

01:08:25.184 --> 01:08:28.062
If you two aren't a real family,
then who in the world is?

01:08:37.739 --> 01:08:39.532
What are you doing? Bend over.

01:08:40.241 --> 01:08:43.328
Make sure you rinse it properly.

01:08:43.411 --> 01:08:45.538
It all got into my eyes.

01:08:48.124 --> 01:08:51.169
I'm doing a pretty good job,
so stop complaining.

01:08:51.252 --> 01:08:53.838
I should just go take a shower instead.

01:09:17.987 --> 01:09:19.572
I'm ready, so talk.

01:09:20.865 --> 01:09:22.200
Ready for what?

01:09:23.951 --> 01:09:28.623
I'm ready to listen to whatever
you have to say, so go ahead.

01:09:32.794 --> 01:09:34.545
Should I just go first?

01:09:38.049 --> 01:09:40.009
I lied because I was embarrassed.

01:09:40.093 --> 01:09:41.219
What?

01:09:42.303 --> 01:09:46.391
Before, I said I lied because
I didn't want you to be embarrassed.

01:09:47.725 --> 01:09:50.728
But honestly, I lied
because I'm the one who was embarrassed.

01:09:52.355 --> 01:09:55.858
I was flustered because no one's
ever asked what my job was before.

01:09:55.942 --> 01:09:58.945
Everyone in Duson-ri knows
that I'm unemployed.

01:09:59.028 --> 01:10:01.322
And I pretended to be Mi-rae in Seoul.

01:10:02.699 --> 01:10:05.410
If you'd said I was just a friend,
I might not have lied.

01:10:05.493 --> 01:10:06.536
But as your girlfriend,

01:10:06.619 --> 01:10:08.955
I couldn't bring myself
to say I'm unemployed.

01:10:11.290 --> 01:10:12.500
I'm sorry I'm like this.

01:10:13.126 --> 01:10:15.586
There are so many things
I have never done,

01:10:15.670 --> 01:10:17.922
so there's a lot that I don't know.

01:10:18.965 --> 01:10:21.926
I didn't even know
we were a couple until then.

01:10:23.136 --> 01:10:24.804
We weren't a couple?

01:10:24.887 --> 01:10:28.599
How would I know?
I've never dated anyone before.

01:10:28.683 --> 01:10:31.561
We were hanging out like it was a date,

01:10:31.644 --> 01:10:34.439
but since you were so quiet,
I assumed you were bored.

01:10:34.522 --> 01:10:36.733
It seemed like you were in a bad mood.

01:10:36.816 --> 01:10:40.862
I felt like you saw me as one
of those restaurants that had shut down.

01:10:41.821 --> 01:10:43.281
I was sick that day.

01:10:45.658 --> 01:10:46.868
You were sick?

01:10:47.452 --> 01:10:49.120
From straining yourself that day?

01:10:49.829 --> 01:10:52.415
I wasn't feeling great
even before I left for Seoul.

01:10:53.833 --> 01:10:55.918
I had a fever, and my body ached.

01:10:56.627 --> 01:11:00.840
Did you catch a cold that night
when you were waiting for me?

01:11:00.923 --> 01:11:02.759
Why didn't you tell me?

01:11:03.551 --> 01:11:05.011
I didn't want to be a burden.

01:11:05.595 --> 01:11:06.596
What?

01:11:07.346 --> 01:11:09.932
I got sick just because
I was outside for a while.

01:11:10.558 --> 01:11:13.311
I couldn't even wander around with you
like you wanted.

01:11:14.312 --> 01:11:16.147
When we were choosing a destination,

01:11:16.230 --> 01:11:19.442
you first had to check
if there were any hills or stairs.

01:11:20.151 --> 01:11:23.654
In the future, there will be more days
when I'm a burden to you.

01:11:24.238 --> 01:11:26.282
So at least for our first date…

01:11:29.118 --> 01:11:31.078
I just wanted to be a normal boyfriend.

01:11:35.416 --> 01:11:37.293
I criticized you for lying

01:11:37.376 --> 01:11:41.756
when I couldn't even bring myself
to tell you that I wasn't feeling well.

01:11:44.550 --> 01:11:45.676
I'm sorry.

01:11:49.347 --> 01:11:51.641
I'm sorry too.

01:11:57.480 --> 01:12:00.942
It's a little late, but I look forward
to spending time with you.

01:12:36.227 --> 01:12:38.479
Maybe what I really wanted

01:12:39.272 --> 01:12:41.566
wasn't to become a perfect person or pair,

01:12:42.567 --> 01:12:44.652
but rather a complete whole.

01:12:46.571 --> 01:12:48.573
Broken pieces that embrace each other

01:12:49.740 --> 01:12:51.868
and make up for each other's shortcomings…

01:12:53.369 --> 01:12:56.122
somehow become one unconventional whole.

01:13:03.004 --> 01:13:04.088
Hey, there.

01:13:04.755 --> 01:13:07.216
What did you want to talk about?
I'm nervous.

01:13:08.634 --> 01:13:10.386
I've been thinking…

01:13:11.012 --> 01:13:13.472
about that option you mentioned before.

01:13:13.556 --> 01:13:15.933
Hold on. Let me take this call.

01:13:16.017 --> 01:13:18.269
I'll be right back. Warm up by the heater.

01:13:22.189 --> 01:13:24.275
Hello? Yes.

01:13:33.910 --> 01:13:35.745
TO: MI-RAE
FROM: SECRET SANTA

01:13:36.370 --> 01:13:39.415
Well, look who it is! Yu Candy is here!

01:13:40.583 --> 01:13:42.209
Where did Se-jin go?

01:13:42.293 --> 01:13:44.337
He went to take a quick phone call.

01:13:44.420 --> 01:13:45.630
I see.

01:13:46.213 --> 01:13:50.217
Are you planning to take over this place?

01:13:50.301 --> 01:13:51.636
- Pardon?
- You're not?

01:13:51.719 --> 01:13:54.722
I heard Se-jin is looking
for someone to take over after him.

01:13:55.222 --> 01:13:57.058
- Someone to take over?
- He didn't tell you?

01:13:57.141 --> 01:14:00.061
He said he doesn't think he'll be able
to finish this year's farming.

01:14:00.144 --> 01:14:02.313
So he's looking for someone to take over.

01:14:02.396 --> 01:14:05.566
Why did he make such a fuss
about those new varieties

01:14:05.650 --> 01:14:09.153
when he wasn't even going
to see things through?

01:14:09.236 --> 01:14:11.238
He's so fickle.

01:14:11.322 --> 01:14:14.700
Why can't he see things through?

01:14:14.784 --> 01:14:16.994
I don't know.
I didn't get all the details.

01:14:17.078 --> 01:14:21.832
I think he's going to the States
to start working again or something.

01:14:26.379 --> 01:14:28.422
Excuse me.

01:14:31.342 --> 01:14:32.551
You're leaving?

01:14:34.804 --> 01:14:36.305
I should've taken you home.

01:14:37.181 --> 01:14:39.350
That would be silly.

01:14:39.850 --> 01:14:42.853
Why would you take me home again
when I already walked you home?

01:14:42.937 --> 01:14:45.523
We would be going back and forth.

01:14:46.482 --> 01:14:48.192
I'm almost home now.

01:14:49.193 --> 01:14:51.570
I'll shower and call you again after.

01:14:51.654 --> 01:14:52.697
Okay.

01:14:59.495 --> 01:15:00.663
You scared me.

01:15:02.623 --> 01:15:04.250
Tae-i?

01:15:04.333 --> 01:15:06.252
What brings you here?

01:15:06.335 --> 01:15:07.878
We need to talk.

01:15:08.462 --> 01:15:10.631
What do you want
to talk about at this hour?

01:15:12.216 --> 01:15:14.135
And how did you know where I live?

01:15:14.927 --> 01:15:18.097
It's something I couldn't talk about
at work or over the phone.

01:15:18.889 --> 01:15:21.517
Why would you talk about
something like that with me?

01:15:23.728 --> 01:15:26.522
I don't know what it's about,

01:15:26.605 --> 01:15:30.818
but it's too late right now.
Let's talk tomorrow during the day.

01:15:31.861 --> 01:15:33.571
I'm Kim Su-yeon's younger brother.

01:15:38.826 --> 01:15:39.952
Pardon?

01:15:40.036 --> 01:15:41.287
My older sister is Kim Su-yeon,

01:15:41.370 --> 01:15:43.581
the Senior Specialist
who left the company.

01:15:51.338 --> 01:15:52.339
What?

01:15:53.632 --> 01:15:55.593
Mi-rae agreed to back out that easily?

01:15:55.676 --> 01:15:56.844
To be honest,

01:15:57.720 --> 01:16:00.431
it wasn't an easy decision for her.

01:16:01.807 --> 01:16:03.434
But when I begged her,

01:16:04.101 --> 01:16:05.478
she fortunately agreed.

01:16:08.105 --> 01:16:09.857
Good work, Mr. Park.

01:16:11.400 --> 01:16:13.694
This wasn't the original plan,

01:16:14.570 --> 01:16:16.614
but somehow things went sideways.

01:16:18.074 --> 01:16:20.284
You heard that
the contractor has been decided, right?

01:16:20.367 --> 01:16:22.870
Yes, I heard
Sihan Construction was selected.

01:16:23.829 --> 01:16:26.499
The project has gotten even bigger
than I thought.

01:16:27.541 --> 01:16:29.794
- We can't afford to have any issues.
- Yes, sir.

01:16:29.877 --> 01:16:33.047
We should've gotten rid
of any potential risks

01:16:33.130 --> 01:16:34.840
before finalizing the contractor.

01:16:35.883 --> 01:16:39.011
If you're talking about Ms. Yu…

01:16:40.513 --> 01:16:43.766
I don't think
you need to worry, given her personality.

01:16:43.849 --> 01:16:45.518
You have no idea, do you?

01:16:45.601 --> 01:16:48.020
She's been acting strange
ever since you went abroad.

01:16:48.104 --> 01:16:49.647
Don't you think so, sir?

01:16:50.189 --> 01:16:52.817
- She does seem different from usual.
- Gosh.

01:16:52.900 --> 01:16:54.443
We need to transfer Mi-rae

01:16:54.527 --> 01:16:56.445
to the Childal Branch
before she causes trouble.

01:16:56.529 --> 01:16:58.197
I don't know what's gotten into her.

01:16:58.280 --> 01:17:01.450
She used to just stare at the wall,
but now she's a different person.

01:17:03.953 --> 01:17:07.039
Maybe there are two people
that look like one.

01:17:08.749 --> 01:17:10.126
What do you mean?

01:17:11.585 --> 01:17:16.048
I heard that Ms. Yu has a twin.

01:17:16.841 --> 01:17:17.842
An identical twin.

01:17:18.467 --> 01:17:19.677
A twin?

01:17:48.539 --> 01:17:51.167
Ms. Yu, can we talk?

01:17:51.250 --> 01:17:52.209
Ms. Yu.

01:17:52.918 --> 01:17:55.004
You're not busy right now, are you?

01:17:55.087 --> 01:17:56.213
Come with me.

01:18:04.555 --> 01:18:07.850
SECURITY OFFICE
EMERGENCY RESPONSE ROOM

01:18:13.022 --> 01:18:14.398
What is it?

01:18:15.566 --> 01:18:17.860
It's nothing. I'm just amazed.

01:18:19.195 --> 01:18:20.070
RESTRICTED AREA

01:18:20.154 --> 01:18:21.864
Why are we
at the data processing room?

01:18:21.947 --> 01:18:25.326
The director said there's something
he needs to check in the call recordings.

01:18:25.409 --> 01:18:26.994
Hello, sir.

01:18:27.578 --> 01:18:29.955
I'm sorry to bother you
so early in the morning.

01:18:33.959 --> 01:18:35.753
What are you waiting for? Scan it.

01:18:38.130 --> 01:18:39.048
Pardon?

01:18:39.131 --> 01:18:40.171
DATA PROCESSING ROOM

01:18:40.257 --> 01:18:41.342
Scan your fingerprint.

01:18:46.972 --> 01:18:50.017
Why are you asking me to do it
when you can do it?

01:18:51.435 --> 01:18:53.187
My finger's like this, so I can't.

01:18:54.647 --> 01:18:55.898
Hurry up and scan it.

01:18:59.193 --> 01:19:00.361
What?

01:19:03.447 --> 01:19:04.782
Did you hurt finger too?

01:19:05.824 --> 01:19:06.867
Or…

01:19:08.202 --> 01:19:10.204
is there another reason why you can't?

01:19:42.528 --> 01:19:43.696
YU MI-JI

01:19:43.779 --> 01:19:45.406
If this is true, it'll be chaos.

01:19:45.489 --> 01:19:47.866
Did you upload that post
to the anonymous forum?

01:19:47.950 --> 01:19:50.331
- About what?
- Reporting the company.

01:19:50.411 --> 01:19:51.662
Why do I have to fight?

01:19:51.761 --> 01:19:53.411
You said you needed to tell me something.

01:19:53.486 --> 01:19:55.207
Why can't I reach you?
Did something happen?

01:19:55.291 --> 01:19:58.836
Have you heard of an adult guardianship?

01:19:58.919 --> 01:20:02.006
I'll give you a bit of money
for the trouble, so please think about it.

01:20:02.089 --> 01:20:03.299
If you're going back

01:20:03.382 --> 01:20:05.801
because you got nowhere to stay,
then sleep here.

01:20:06.343 --> 01:20:09.221
May I take a look?
Your old hairstyle was pretty too.

01:20:09.305 --> 01:20:11.265
It looked pretty even when it was shorter.

01:20:11.348 --> 01:20:12.975
You look pretty.

01:20:18.186 --> 01:20:20.186
Subtitle translation by Jane Jung
